meta {
  name: Create purchase
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/purchases
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "userId": 1,
    "paymentStatus": "PENDING",
    "taxes": 2.99,
    "discountAmount": 0,
    "reference": "WEB-1001",
    "products": [
      {
        "productId": 1,
        "quantity": 2
      }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  # Create a purchase

  Orders with their product lines. Totals are computed by the server from each product's current price and are never accepted from the client: each line's `amount` is `price × quantity`, `totalAmount` is the sum of the lines, and `finalAmount` is `totalAmount + taxes − discountAmount`, floored at 0. Quantities and unit prices are kept in `data.lines`. After creation only `reference`, `paymentStatus`, `fulfillmentStatus`, `invoice`, `paymentDate` and `data` can change. `fulfillmentStatus` tracks shipping (`PENDING` → `SHIPPED` → `DELIVERED`, or `CANCELLED`) apart from payment.

  The server fills `created` with an audit stamp (`client`, `server`, `serverDate`, `serverTime` in APP_TIMEZONE, `unixTime`, `user`, `role` from the token). `status`, `statusName`, `created`, `updated`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt` and any other undeclared key are ignored if sent. An optional top-level `time` (ISO string) is recorded as `created.client`.

  ## Auth

  Bearer token of a user whose role is `ADMIN` (send **auth/Log in** first; it stores `{{token}}`).

  ## Body (JSON)

  | Field | Type | Required | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `userId` | integer | yes on create | Id of an existing user. |
  | `paymentStatus` | string | yes on create | One of `PENDING`, `SUCCESS`, `FAILED`, `REJECTED`. |
  | `fulfillmentStatus` | string | no | One of `PENDING`, `SHIPPED`, `DELIVERED`, `CANCELLED`; defaults to `PENDING`. |
  | `products` | array | yes on create | 1–100 lines of `{ productId: integer, quantity: integer 1–999 }`; each product must exist and be active. Create only. |
  | `taxes` | number | no | ≥ 0; defaults to 0. Create only. |
  | `discountAmount` | number | no | ≥ 0; defaults to 0. Create only. |
  | `reference` | string \| null | no | Max 100 characters. |
  | `invoice` | string \| null | no | Max 100 characters. |
  | `paymentDate` | string (ISO date) \| null | no | When payment was taken. |
  | `data` | object \| null | no | Free-form metadata; the server adds `lines`. |

  ## Responses

  ### 201 Created

    {
      "message": "Purchase created",
      "data": {
        "id": 1,
        "userId": 1,
        "reference": "WEB-1001",
        "totalAmount": "29.9",
        "taxes": "2.99",
        "discountAmount": "0",
        "finalAmount": "32.89",
        "paymentStatus": "PENDING",
        "fulfillmentStatus": "PENDING",
        "invoice": null,
        "paymentDate": null,
        "data": {
          "lines": [
            {
              "productId": 1,
              "quantity": 2,
              "unitPrice": "14.95"
            }
          ]
        },
        "user": {
          "id": 1,
          "name": "Store",
          "lastName": "Administrator",
          "email": "admin@lpaecomms.test"
        },
        "products": [
          {
            "id": 1,
            "purchaseId": 1,
            "productId": 1,
            "amount": "29.9",
            "product": {
              "id": 1,
              "name": "Wireless Headphones",
              "code": "wireless-headphones"
            }
          }
        ],
        "created": {
          "client": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
          "server": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
          "serverDate": "2026-09-27",
          "serverTime": "12:30:14",
          "unixTime": 1790476214,
          "user": 1,
          "role": "ADMIN"
        },
        "updated": null,
        "statusName": "ACTIVE",
        "status": 1,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z"
      },
      "pagination": null
    }

  ### 400 Bad Request — validation failed

  A body field is missing or invalid; one `errors` entry per field. Also returned when a referenced id does not exist (`userId`). For purchases, also when a product is missing, inactive or a draft.

    {
      "message": "Some fields need attention.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": [
        {
          "field": "userId",
          "message": "Invalid input"
        }
      ]
    }

  ### 401 Unauthorized — missing, invalid or expired token

    {
      "message": "Sign in to continue.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  ### 403 Forbidden — the token's role is not ADMIN

    {
      "message": "You do not have permission to do this.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  Outside production, error bodies also carry `stack`.
}
